        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Shawl of printed silk and wool. Woven with a white silk warp and white wool weft, except for one inch wide bands of silk weft at intervals of about a foot (12 inches). The broad woollen bands are printed in red, blue, green, yellow and black with meandering stems of tiny leaves and flowers and a semi-eastern motif from which spring stems of flowers. An applied knotted silk fringe in white, pink, mustard and lilac is on all four sides of the square shawl."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/27d6d734-50f7-34ff-b9be-35236b8ac248> .

